SUMMARY:Sustainable Balcony Gardening
DESCRIPTION:Join us and learn how to bring your balcony to life!\n \nLearn about the inspiring beauty and practical benefits of gardening on your balcony with a focus on native plants. You will leave with the know-how to bring your small outdoor space to life. Learn about plant selection\, watering\, maintenance\, maximising your sun exposure and more.\n \nThursday\, June 18\, 6 to 7:30 p.m.\n \nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Toronto and Region Conservation Authority (TRCA)\n \nToronto and Region Conservation Authority (TRCA) is one of 36 Conservation Authorities in Ontario. They:\n\n\n\nTake care of nine watersheds and the Lake Ontario shoreline\, in partnership with municipalities\, the Province\, and community members\,\nWork to preserve and protect the land\,\nMonitor and report on the health of the environment in the Toronto Region\,\nEngage communities and encourage people of all ages to get outside and enjoy nature!\n\nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member! \nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/sustainable-balcony-gardening/
